SFGOP: Reopen the VirtIO framebuffer after a mode change

Read the VirtIO framebuffer generation around the mode, pixel layout and mapping in SFGOPOpen and open again when it moved. Each connection keeps the generation it opened at until SFGOPClose. SFGOPRefresh closes and reopens when the driver published a new framebuffer, so the old mapping goes with its connection.

